; PAUSE/CONTINUE, BACKTRACE, EXECTIME: a real debugging toolkit,
; adapted from Terrapin's PAUSE/CONTINUE(CO)/BACKTRACE(BT)/EXECTIME.
;
; PAUSE genuinely halts the script and busy-waits for a live CONTINUE --
; it only makes sense run from the actual app (a real entry box to type
; CONTINUE into), not the headless test driver, where it's a silent
; no-op instead of hanging forever.

TO spiral :size
  IF :size > 200 [STOP]
  FD :size
  RT 91

  IF :size = 50 [
    BACKTRACE          ; shows this call, recursively, back to the top
    PAUSE              ; halts right here -- try PRINT :size, or SETPENCOLOR
                       ; 255 0 0, before typing CONTINUE to resume
  ]

  spiral :size + 2
END

PRINT EXECTIME [spiral 10]   ; how long the whole (paused!) call took
